Ladybird masks transformed text by grapheme, retaining a mapping to the
DOM source. Blink’s LayoutText::TransformAndSecureText() applies casing
before SecureText(). WebKit selects its masking glyph in RenderText and
applies it in secureText(). Gecko’s nsTextFrame obtains the glyph from
TextSecurityMaskChar() for the text run.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79 and WebKit 26.5 rendered two marks for an
uppercased German sharp s. Firefox 151.0 rendered one. The three
browsers used distinct disc, circle and square marks.
